# .env.example — what Docker Compose reads. Copy to .env and fill in.
#
# This file is deliberately small. The Lab application has its own environment
# file at apps/lab/.env (and apps/lab/.env.example), which is where every
# application key lives. Each tool reads its own file; that is the convention.
#
# The one value these two files share is the Lab database password below, which
# must equal DB_PASSWORD in apps/lab/.env. scripts/verify-lab-app.sh asserts it.

# --- Lab database (PostgreSQL 17 + pgvector, container on 127.0.0.1:5433) ---
# Empty in the template. docker compose fails loudly if unset — there is no default.
LAB_DB_PASSWORD=
